-- title:
--   Other cusps avoid the ∞-cusp prime on the pole chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5\le q$ and a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the field `xHFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH (q^2*M') H)` of rational $\mathsf q$-expansions, where $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, acting on $K$ compatibly with the tower $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be non-zero with Laurent series the image of the rational $j$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under `coeffEmb L`. Then for every minimal prime $P$ over the ideal of the pole chart algebra `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A ↥K j` (by definition `chartAlg A ↥K {j⁻¹}`) generated by the element $j^{-1}$, namely `jInvChartInf A ↥K j`: if $P$ contains some element whose $\mathsf q$-expansion has non-zero constant coefficient, then $P$ contains an element $b$ whose constant coefficient $((b:K):L((\mathsf q))).\mathrm{coeff}\,0$ is not the image of any element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   This is the separation of the cusps of $X_H(q^2M')$ at the $\mathsf q$-adic cusp $\infty$ over the base $A$: a minimal prime of $(1/j)$ on the pole chart which is not the $\mathsf q$-adic cusp is not contained in the prime $\{b: b(0)\in\mathfrak m_A\}$ cutting out the cusp $\infty$ in the special fibre. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_cuspInfty_xH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_cuspInfty_xH), the regularity of the pole chart localised at the cusp $\infty$.
